      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a 2022 F-150 with some slipping issues in the transmission. My scan tool is showing some really weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit during the shifts. What are the most likely culprits for these kinds of pressure fluctuations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most likely culprits for irregular hydraulic pressure spikes in your 2022 F-150 transmission are a failing pressure relief valve, a worn or stuck shift solenoid, or internal valve pack wear causing erratic fluid flow. These components are responsible for regulating pressure during shifts, and their malfunctions can create the specific \"spikes\" your scan tool is detecting, often leading to slips. Additionally, low fluid level or degraded fluid quality can exacerbate these issues by reducing hydraulic consistency. It is recommended to inspect the solenoids and check for external leaks before considering internal transmission service. Given the complexity, consulting a specialized technician familiar with Ford 10T transmissions is advisable for accurate diagnosis.",
