      "role": "user",
      "content": "the solenoids seem okay on the visual inspection but the spikes are so inconsistent. it's like it happens randomly one minute and then smooth the next. could there be something clogging the lines or just some weird mechanical glitch causing the erratic pressure?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, erratic pressure spikes that appear and disappear randomly are often caused by internal mechanical faults rather than just clogged lines. Specific issues like a worn spool in the valve body, a distressed clutch pack, or a failing metering sleeve can cause these fluctuations as the symptoms intensify or abate due to wear. A clog might cause a steady over-pressure issue, whereas a mechanical failure inside the transmission usually results in the inconsistent behavior you are seeing. You likely need to perform an NDA (No-Dump Test) scan or perform a bounce test to isolate the specific pressure circuit causing these glitches.",
